“Sleigh Ride” from The Ronettes enters the top 10 of the Hot 100, while Dean Martin rises and “Jungle Bell Rock” and Kelly Clarkson slip a spot. Will Brenda Lee take No. 1 this week?&nbsp;

Tetris Kelly:

This is the Billboard Hot 100 top 10 for the week dated January 3. Joining the top 10 is &#8220;Sleigh Ride.&#8221; Andy Williams is still at nine. Kelly Clarkson slips to No. 8. Dean Martin storms to seven. Nat &#8220;King&#8221; Cole is locked at six, so is &#8220;Santa Tell Me&#8221; at No. 5, and &#8220;Last Christmas&#8221; at No. 4. &#8220;Jingle Bell Rock&#8221; is down to three, while Brenda Lee moves up to No. 2. And grabbing a record extending 22nd week at No. 1 is Mariah Carey&#8217;s &#8220;All I Want For Christmas Is You.&#8221;

